WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.252 --> 00:00:01.992
- This is Mr. Mac.

00:00:01.992 --> 00:00:03.668
He's an Aldabra Tortoise,

00:00:03.668 --> 00:00:05.546
a giant tortoise species that can live

00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:08.656
past 180 and may have
the longest life span

00:00:08.656 --> 00:00:11.338
of any creature on the planet.

00:00:11.338 --> 00:00:14.255
(orchestral music)

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:18.593
Hailing from the Aldabra Atoll,

00:00:18.593 --> 00:00:21.545
a small cluster of coral
islands in the Indian Ocean,

00:00:21.545 --> 00:00:24.212
the Aldabra Tortoise is massive.

00:00:25.456 --> 00:00:28.103
Endowed with a domed shell, long neck,

00:00:28.103 --> 00:00:30.670
and strong claws, they
can grow to be longer

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:35.160
than four feet and can
weigh as much as 500 pounds.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.945
They live in grasslands
and subsist on a diet

00:00:37.945 --> 00:00:41.296
of dry, nutrient rich vegetation.

00:00:41.296 --> 00:00:43.116
An Aldabra Tortoise has never met

00:00:43.116 --> 00:00:45.033
a blade of grass it didn't like.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.541
And it won't be deterred from eating it

00:00:46.541 --> 00:00:49.469
even if it takes a while to reach it.

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:51.515
But the tortoises have had a harder time

00:00:51.515 --> 00:00:54.139
finding food because
of habitat destruction

00:00:54.139 --> 00:00:58.222
caused by humans and
increasingly climate change.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.941
This is the Aldabra Tortoise.

00:01:01.941 --> 00:01:05.024
(orchestral fanfare)

